   "note": "NEGATIVE RESULT, recorded so the candidate is not re-offered. Leaf 9 -- which phase 0b classified as this volume's title page, and from which it read the year 1837 -- is an ADVERTISEMENT: Samuel J. Sigler, looking-glass and picture-frame manufacturer, on the 'BROOKLYN DIRECTORY ADVERTISER' page (printed p.11), boasting 'ESTABLISHED 1837'. This is the exact case SURVEY_PLAN.md documents, now confirmed by eye; YEAR_VETO suppresses it. The real title page was not located: leaves 22/25/28 are also advertiser pages (p.27 at leaf 25), and this volume's printed numbering restarts deep in the book -- IA puts printed p.2 at leaf 396 -- so the front advertising section is very long. Finding it needs a targeted search, not the 30-leaf front window."
